# Fasting: "If you would begin your draw step, you may skip that step instead. If you do, you gain 2 life." Declined, the
# draw step happens: Bot1 draws, gains no life, and "when you draw a card, destroy this enchantment" destroys it (CR
# 701.8a). Bot2's draw step on turn 2 is not Fasting's to skip ("your draw step": Bot2 is never asked), and Bot2's draw,
# with Fasting on the battlefield, destroys nothing: only its controller's draw does. The skip is chosen as the draw step
# would begin (the ruling), after the upkeep's hunger counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Fasting
Mox Pearl
Plains x5
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fasting.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Accept
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Fasting.Counters.Hunger = (absent)
Bot1.Decline
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Fasting = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Fasting
